# Screens for the TPS Report Generator Reference and Operating Procedures
# (1024-3300-12), bead initech-ipu5.14.  name|serial marker[#count]|disk
# Every screen takes the JOURNEY route (disk `flair`, pubs/screens/capture.sh):
# the flagship image boots to the FLAIR desktop, the locked trace of
# test-flair-exit-to-dos leaves it through Special > Exit to InitechDOS, and
# the keystrokes of screens/NAME.keys are typed at the A:\> prompt -- the
# ONLY keyboard source.  Each .keys starts with the two Enters that answer
# the date and time prompts and with CLS (the seconds of the time prompt
# depend on how long the desktop takes to go).  The marker is the prompt the
# session ends on, #count its occurrences on the serial mirror.
# Regenerate with "make pubs-screens"; "make test-pubs-screens" re-captures
# every screen and diffs it against the book.
# DRAFT (lane tpsr2, bead initech-5igf): r2align, r5cover and r5refuse are
# hand-written .draft transcripts of the DECIDED R2/R5 wording and are not
# listed here; after tpsr2 merges, add their rows and capture them, and
# re-capture every screen that passes R2 (tpsritual, tpsdone, tpsbak).
tpsstart|A:\APPS>#2|flair
tpsdir|A:\APPS>#2|flair
tpsroot|A:\>#3|flair
tps001|A:\>#3|flair
tps007|A:\APPS>#2|flair
tps006|A:\APPS>#2|flair
tps002|A:\>#4|flair
tpsritual|A:\APPS>#2|flair
tpsdone|A:\APPS>#2|flair
tpsbak|A:\APPS>#4|flair
